    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d83">

                <pb facs="0085" n="71" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg71"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.24/1145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-10-13T18:00:00-04:00">October 13, 1942—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1698. Confirming my conversation this afternoon with Duggan.<anchor n="91"
                        xml:id="d83-f1"/> Your telegram 1221, October 12, 2 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >11</hi>] p.m.</p>
                <p>Instructions came from Ministry of War Brazil for purchase through Merry del Val
                    Company and conveyed to me by Brazilian Ambassador. In your telegram No. 1121,
                    September 25, 8 p.m. you said Metals Reserve had agreed to instruct Anaconda to
                    sell amount asked, and I so informed the Ambassador. Your No. 1221 puts me in a
                    most embarrassing position since my relations with Brazilian Ambassador are very
                    close and constant and it happens that Merry del Val is his son-in-law. I feel
                    strongly that it will be a serious mistake to ignore your No. 1121 at this stage
                    and result in resentment of Ambassador with whom it is of the utmost importance
                    that I <pb facs="0086" n="72" xml:id="pg72"/> maintain the closest and
                    friendliest relations. There seems no doubt that the order is genuine and from
                    Brazil’s Ministry of War. Whatever may result in the future urge that this one
                    order be put through.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d83-f1" n="91" xml:id="d83-f1-content">
                <p>Laurence Duggan, Adviser on Political Relations.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
